   "notes": "Chris Adams House (formerly Botolph House), 17 Botolph Lane, Pembroke College: Georgian three-bay house, painted white over brick, 6/6 sashes on the first and second floors, a centre door with pilastered doorcase and radial fanlight, ground-floor sashes with louvred shutters (shutters not modelled), green plaque, white band at first-floor level. From a frontal 2017 Mapillary view across the Botolph Lane junction; the facade starts at the east (p0) corner, bay positions scaled from the door width; the west end is hidden behind no. 15."
